kwbackup (0.99.26) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fix(rclone): stream rclone output under --verbose so --progress is visible

    rclone was always started with capture_output=True, so its progress and stats
    went into a captured stderr and were dropped unless the command failed. The
    --progress flag added in 0.99.25 was therefore invisible.

    run() now has capture=True/False. Rclone.run streams by default when VERBOSE
    is on and keeps capture for lsf, whose stdout must be parsed. A failed
    streamed command still reports the command and the exit code.

    tests: the fake rclone writes a progress line to stderr when --progress is
    present; it is hidden by default, visible with --verbose and --debug (26/26).

