kwbackup (0.99.25) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(cli): --verbose also makes rclone talk, --debug owns the debug log

    --verbose used to raise the script log to debug, which flooded the output,
    and it did not affect rclone at all. Now:

      --verbose  log stays at info, rclone gets --progress (stats + progress)
      --debug    log at debug (every command and its arguments), rclone --progress

    The rclone flag is added in Rclone._base(), so it applies to lsf, copyto,
    sync and deletefile alike. Neither flag changes behaviour, only output.

    tests: default run has no --progress and no command lines, --verbose adds
    --progress but keeps debug off, --debug adds both (26/26).

